# Shared by every image build in this repository. Three Dockerfiles build with
# the repo root as context -- Dockerfile (operator), Dockerfile.external-runtime,
# and the sample-game module images under examples/ -- so anything a COPY in any
# of them touches must stay in the context.
#
# In particular examples/ is NOT excluded: the demo module images are built as
# `docker build -f examples/.../Dockerfile .` and copy the sample game's own
# go.mod. Excluding it breaks the e2e smoke test, which builds those images.
#
# What remains here is inert for every build: docs, deployment manifests, and
# local tooling state. The context grew substantially when the operator and the
# external runtime merged, and docs/ alone carries the research pack plus ~70
# dispatch receipts.

.git
.github
.claude
.sprintctl
.kctl
.auditctl
.tools

# Docs and dispatch records.
docs
verification
*.md
project.toml
bindery-core.dispatch.json

# Deployment manifests: consumed by helm/kubectl, never copied into an image.
helm
charts
k8s
config

# Local build and test artifacts.
bin
dist
coverage*.out
*.test
.gocache
.cache
